        "title": "CLI binary build adds local build flag to skip keychain",
        "summary": "The binary build script now injects `CODEBUFF_LOCAL_BUILD` into the compiled CLI, setting it to 'true' for builds outside GitHub Actions. This flag is read by the auth token store to keep the credential in the local file instead of the OS keychain, which prevents ad-hoc signature mismatch prompts on macOS during local development. The flag is wired through the CLI environment type and helper.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In `cli/scripts/build-binary.ts`, a new define flag `CODEBUFF_LOCAL_BUILD` is set to 'true' when `GITHUB_ACTIONS` is not 'true'. In `cli/src/utils/auth-token-store.ts`, `resolveSecretStore` now returns `null` (keeping the token in the file) when `CODEBUFF_LOCAL_BUILD` is 'true'.",
