        "calls": 1,
        "text": "The Freebuff team added a quiet switch to their internal build tools so that software copies created on personal computers instead of company servers keep your sign-in code in a private file rather than asking your computer for a password every time you make a new copy. This change only affects the team members who manually build and test the software on their own machines to catch problems before releases. Regular users who download the official software from the website experience no change, and this internal safety measure does not affect how the service runs for anyone else.",
